  {"id":"constitute ARTICLE 7","source":"constitute","country":"IRL","instrument":"Ireland 1937 (rev. 2019)","kind":"constitution","article":"ARTICLE 7","part":"article","lang":"en","topics":["symbols"],"text":"The national flag is the tricolour of green, white and orange.","url":"https://www.constituteproject.org/service/html?cons_id=Ireland_2019&lang=en","fetched":"2026-11-12","sha256":"59d69fff564a037bfb8579a7d5a7615f470bf5d35d365f4a1d525abcf178c8e5"},
  {"id":"constitute ARTICLE 40, 2","source":"constitute","country":"IRL","instrument":"Ireland 1937 (rev. 2019)","kind":"constitution","article":"ARTICLE 40, 2","part":"article","lang":"en","topics":["honours"],"text":"Titles of nobility shall not be conferred by the State. No title of nobility or of honour may be accepted by any citizen except with the prior approval of the Government.","url":"https://www.constituteproject.org/service/html?cons_id=Ireland_2019&lang=en","fetched":"2026-11-12","sha256":"5b015452a21576da06f72fcb178731d0cf2a0bf26862946949ee5fd0cae00f7d"},
  {"id":"constitute ARTICLE 40, 3","source":"constitute","country":"IRL","instrument":"Ireland 1937 (rev. 2019)","kind":"constitution","article":"ARTICLE 40, 3","part":"article","lang":"en","topics":["defamation"],"text":"The State guarantees in its laws to respect, and, as far as practicable, by its laws to defend and vindicate the personal rights of the citizen. The State shall, in particular, by its laws protect as best it may from unjust attack and, in the case of injustice done, vindicate the life, person, good name, and property rights of every citizen. Provision may be made by law for the regulation of termination of pregnancy.","url":"https://www.constituteproject.org/service/html?cons_id=Ireland_2019&lang=en","fetched":"2026-11-12","sha256":"af32d7c929d59a7377f63fcfcce885a44a9777d2edd3de284f3803b1ed4e2ba0"}
